  transmission_colour uuid [note: 'The transmissive part of the reflectance equation can be given as either a colour or a scalar factor.; ref to any; source: IfcSurfaceStyleRendering attribute 2: OPTIONAL IfcColourOrFactor; via select IfcColourOrFactor']
  diffuse_transmission_colour uuid [note: 'The diffuse transmission part of the reflectance equation can be given as either a colour or a scalar factor.; ref to any; source: IfcSurfaceStyleRendering attribute 3: OPTIONAL IfcColourOrFactor; via select IfcColourOrFactor']
  reflection_colour uuid [note: 'The reflection (or mirror) part of the reflectance equation can be given as either a colour or a scalar factor.; ref to any; source: IfcSurfaceStyleRendering attribute 4: OPTIONAL IfcColourOrFactor; via select IfcColourOrFactor']
  specular_colour uuid [note: 'In a PHONG ReflectanceMethod, the SpecularColour correlates to the specularColor attribute in the X3D Phong lighting model.; ref to any; source: IfcSurfaceStyleRendering attribute 5: OPTIONAL IfcColourOrFactor; via select IfcColourOrFactor']
  specular_highlight text [note: 'In a PHONG ReflectanceMethod, the SpecularHighlight is specified as a IfcSpecularRoughness and correlates to the inverse of the shininess attribute in the X3D Phong lighting model.; source: IfcSurfaceStyleRendering attribute 6: OPTIONAL IfcSpecularHighlightSelect; SELECT IfcSpecularHighlightSelect of value types, stored as text (the member type tag is not kept)']
  reflectance_method text [not null, note: 'Identifies the predefined types of reflectance method from which the method required may be set.; source: IfcSurfaceStyleRendering attribute 7: IfcReflectanceMethodEnum; enumeration IfcReflectanceMethodEnum']
  Note: 'IfcSurfaceStyleRendering: IfcSurfaceStyleRendering holds the properties for visualization related to a particular surface style.'
